#
# The number of `interfacebloat` findings tolerated in the tree. This is a
# RATCHET: CI fails if the count goes UP, and also fails if it goes DOWN without
# this number being lowered in the same PR. Both directions are deliberate --
# a baseline nobody lowers is a baseline that stops meaning anything.
#
# Why a count and not a per-file list: measured 2026-08-18, the count is stable
# across checkouts and caches (28 from the repo root, 28 from inside a worktree,
# 28 from an isolated clone) while the reported PATHS are not -- golangci-lint's
# result cache is keyed by file content, so an unchanged file replays whichever
# path was recorded first, which for this repo meant paths pointing into sibling
# worktrees. A per-file baseline would have been built on the unstable half of
# the output.
#
# Two ways to go over, both of which leave a reviewable trace:
#   1. Per interface -- `//nolint:interfacebloat // <reason>`. nolintlint is
#      configured with require-explanation and require-specific, so a silent or
#      unexplained override does not compile past the linter.
#   2. Wholesale -- raise the number below. That is a one-line diff in a file
#      whose only purpose is to hold this number, so it cannot land unnoticed.
#
# Baseline set on b7f4627b (2026-08-18) from an isolated clone with a cleared
# golangci-lint cache.
28
